From 5f5bcbe6dcd4761092bbaea32b41be3881832eef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:47:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pixels): tile deltas between two versions of a layer

RasterDelta keeps the 64-pixel tiles of an older raster that differ
from a newer one of the same size, which is all an undo step needs to
rebuild the older pixels. Tiles that were fully transparent cost
nothing; up to 64 other tiles are deflated (a stroke's delta is a few
KB, measured 2-13 KB on 2048 x 2048 layers), more are kept raw so a
whole-layer change stays cheap to build.

The diff scans each tile's part of a row with a branch-free loop until
the tile is marked: about 1.3-4 ms per 2048 x 2048 pair on this VM,
bound by memory bandwidth. Not yet used; the undo history comes next.

