From 9eca139073c7c8650764238990c7d08597779f6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:47:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(history): undo history that keeps deep steps as tile
 deltas

UndoHistory holds undo and redo steps as a document state plus its
pixel planes (layer pixels and masks by PlaneKey). Steps share a plane
while its buffer is unchanged; below the newest step of each stack a
plane is archived as a RasterDelta against the same plane one step
closer to the present and its buffer is released. Undo and redo copy
the nearest full buffer once and lay the deltas over it, then keep the
result, so successive undos rebuild in one step. A plane stays whole
when its delta would not save half of it, when no newer step has the
same plane (deleted layer) or the size changed (resized canvas).

Also: a byte budget that counts only what the history holds beyond the
document's own buffers, runs that merge a slider drag into one step,
a mark that changes on every step/undo/redo/clear, and stepsSince(mark)
for tools that undo their own steps. Undo and redo rebuild before they
touch the stacks, and archiving tolerates running out of memory.

Tested on the JVM against a plain deep-copy history with random edits
(add/remove/reorder/duplicate layers, masks, resizes, property-only
edits) interleaved with undo, redo and new edits.

